# Exception Report — auto resolution comments

When you fix a bug that has (or will create) rows in **Reports → Exception Report**, resolve those exceptions with an automatic resolution comment. Do not leave matching OPEN rows unexplained.

## After a fix lands

Prefer the service helper (same DB session as your verification script):

```python
from app.services.exception_log_service import auto_resolve_by_cursor

auto_resolve_by_cursor(
    db,
    exception_ids=[...],  # preferred when known
    # or message_fragments=("rate limit",), sources={"meta_lead_sync"},
    detail="One sentence on what you changed.",
)
```

Or call the API (authenticated admin):

`POST /api/v1/reports/exception-logs/auto-resolve`
`{"mode":"cursor_agent","exception_ids":[5],"detail":"Fixed page-token lookup off /me/accounts."}`

Or patch a single row with auto comment:

`PATCH /api/v1/reports/exception-logs/{id}/status`
`{"status":"RESOLVED","resolved_by":"cursor_agent","resolution_comment":null}`
(optional `detail` via a non-null `resolution_comment` override)

## Already automatic (do not duplicate)

- **Server recovery** — stranded Meta sync lock recovery auto-resolves “already in progress” rows
- **Successful Meta sync** — auto-resolves open Meta Graph / lead_sync_failure rows
- **Page refresh** — transient UI/network/timeout client exceptions auto-resolve once per tab session

Manual admin Resolve in the UI still requires a typed comment.
